<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1906c470-2279-46f2-9eb3-7b53ea56814d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Range-bearing inputs gate only on HermiT; ELK's range results are informational" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1906c470-2279-46f2-9eb3-7b53ea56814d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1906c470-2279-46f2-9eb3-7b53ea56814d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "In the differential, HermiT gates every comparable input. ELK gates an input only if every census construct in it passes all of ELK's capability probes AND it has no ObjectPropertyRange at all. ELK's diffs on range-bearing inputs are printed for information and never gate.\n\nThis tightens Constraint b293cf6e, which allowed \"ELK only if the pinned version passes the range probe\". ELK 0.6.0's release notes claim only partial ObjectPropertyRange support, and a handful of passing probes doesn't make a partial implementation complete. Gating on it would risk certifying HOWL against an oracle that processed a smaller theory.\n\nMeasured at S3: ELK 0.6.0 passes 4 of the 5 range probes (direct, inherited, induced unsat, no over-derivation). On range plus ABox (r(a,b), range(r)=C, B(b), B disjoint C) it logs its own org.semanticweb.elk.reasoner.completeness.Incompleteness warning, so the harness fails that file for ELK. It does the same on the abox-disjoint-range hazard. corpus/oracle-capabilities.txt records this, and a change fails `make probes` until it's reviewed and regenerated. SPEC §10 item 1 was updated to match." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1906c470-2279-46f2-9eb3-7b53ea56814d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1906c470-2279-46f2-9eb3-7b53ea56814d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T01:25:36.101902Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
