<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Spec SPEC.md approved for implementation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "James Adam approved HOWL's SPEC.md for implementation on 2026-08-17, authorising the capture of its stated Requirements, Constraints and settled ArchitecturalDecisions as accepted records ahead of implementation work.\n\nspec-approval: /Users/jcadam/code/howl/SPEC.md\n\nMinted in this pass (15 records):\n\nRequirements —\n- Coherence validation inside an authoring/CI loop — Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f\n- Defined-class subsumption through existential restrictions — Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2\n- Minimal mapping repair for ontology alignment — Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8\n- New subsumptions against a committed baseline — Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992\n\nConstraints —\n- Reports are input-determined — Constraint/007e982c-4936-4607-8bda-33451359f836\n- A port amendment gates its capability — Constraint/456acb54-a6ff-4970-a062-863892f2825f\n- Classification within 5x ELK under a pinned protocol — Constraint/11c160af-1cdd-477f-9129-c3acd1b88622\n- Expressivity is claimed construct-by-construct, never by label — Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8\n- Differential oracles must be capability-probed per construct — Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7\n\nArchitecturalDecisions —\n- Consequence-based saturation, not tableau — ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52\n- ABox encoding: class assertions to GCIs, role assertions to edges — ArchitecturalDecision/5cecf538-1be2-4f57-a979-888812c3b7d4\n- Profile selection is whole-ontology membership in one profile — ArchitecturalDecision/3eacfa8e-800e-452f-9547-e4ee85c2f45d\n- A collective RBox failure omits the whole RBox — ArchitecturalDecision/83481302-01ca-452f-82a5-b6dc3f338b97\n- HOWL and GROWL compose through RDF, never shared state — ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801\n\nSuperseded —\n- Constraint/8c9b3db7 (which specified range support as a new completion rule CR8) replaced by Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce, ranges by the published elimination construction. This was graph drift: the spec had already removed CR8 and the record still asserted it.\n\nReused rather than re-minted: the port-is-the-deliverable posture (inside Requirement/53e71ad6), the complete-run rule (Constraint/bb86deca), the three coherence definitions (Constraint/c7023d3a), gate-versus-proof (Constraint/ae25e3d4), and Z3-proves-faithfulness (Lesson/2acb7b52).\n\nNote for re-approval: SPEC.md is a living design document that went through fourteen review rounds before approval. Diff it against these records before mining it again." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:30:24.314083Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Spec SPEC.md approved for implementation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bde42ef-92a1-4f07-9071-da1b498203e8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bde42ef-92a1-4f07-9071-da1b498203e8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stage 0 consumes a header node's scaffolding and annotations, never its logical triples" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bde42ef-92a1-4f07-9071-da1b498203e8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bde42ef-92a1-4f07-9071-da1b498203e8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`stage0-header` (src/decode.slop) consumes the triples of header nodes by subject:\n- ontology nodes;\n- `owl:Axiom` reification nodes;\n- `owl:Annotation` nodes (an annotation on an annotation, new in M1 S3).\n\nBut it consumes only what `header-consumable` admits: the node's own `rdf:type` as ontology, axiom or annotation, the annotatedSource/Property/Target scaffolding, header properties, and annotations. A LOGICAL triple on such a node passes through to the decoder, where it becomes an omission. Logical means an OWL/RDFS axiom or class-expression predicate (`logical-predicate`), or any other `rdf:type`.\n\n**Why:** consumption by subject made a mixed node, such as `_:x a owl:Annotation ; rdfs:subClassOf :C`, shrink the input silently. There was no omission and no fault, and the verdict read COHERENT over a document HOWL had not fully read. Found by the second Codex review of M1 S3; the gap had applied to `owl:Axiom` nodes since M0.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- hazards/logical-triple-on-header-node.ttl reports INCONCLUSIVE with the triple as an omission (acceptance exit 2).\n- `test-logical-triple-on-header-node-is-not-swallowed` goes red when the check is removed.\n- Five `@example`s on `header-consumable` run under `make example`.\n- No golden moved, and the RO/OBI/GO report hashes are unchanged." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bde42ef-92a1-4f07-9071-da1b498203e8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bde42ef-92a1-4f07-9071-da1b498203e8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T03:17:02.709887Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
