<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The differential compares HOWL's canonical report; no separate probe binary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The differential harness reads `howl validate --report` directly: the canonical report already is the bottom-compressed entailment dump SPEC §10 asks for. It has `sub A B` for every class B ∈ S(A), including A and ⊤; `sub A owl:Nothing` alone plus `unsat A` for an unsatisfiable A; and only `inconsistent true` under inconsistency. The oracle program (oracle/) writes the same grammar, so corpus/entdiff.py compares sets and decides entails-sub(A,B) for every ordered pair in linear time.\n\nThe roadmap's `howl-probe` binary had two jobs: an entailment dump, and keeping a clock out of the product CLI. S1 did both — the canonical report, and `--timings` on stderr (AD c713b09e). So a separate binary would only be a second output format to keep in step.\n\nThe rule that only a complete run is compared moved INTO the comparator. entdiff refuses (exit 3) any HOWL report without `termination fixpoint` and `omitted 0`, so no driver can diff a partial run by forgetting to check.\n\n`howl-probe pairs` was meant to guard that the port's probe agrees with the dump. It became `test-entails-sub-agrees-with-report` in src/test.slop, over fixtures chosen to hit each disjunct of entails-sub and each representational corner. It goes red when entails-sub drops its inconsistency arm.\n\nMeasured at S3: 54 fixtures (v0, hazards, 26 probes) diff-clean against HermiT, and against ELK wherever routed. Removing CR4-on-pred's S(Y) walk makes both `probes` and `diff-fixtures` report HOWL-missing on the litmus and 8 probes, against both oracles." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T01:25:35.940593Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
