<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6135b9b3-1a57-4eab-9a0a-0ae9994ed5c3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/8cde5c22-1c08-4ad7-a802-62c126cdfef7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7d9facaf-6d1b-4f3f-8cd0-ff223580b686> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7d9facaf-6d1b-4f3f-8cd0-ff223580b686> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule dispatch goes through a premise index built once per run" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7d9facaf-6d1b-4f3f-8cd0-ff223580b686> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7d9facaf-6d1b-4f3f-8cd0-ff223580b686> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`apply-el-rules` no longer receives the axiom list. `build-rule-index` (src/rules/premise.slop) runs once in `prepare` and files every normal-form axiom under the key its §6.4 trigger looks up — CR1 by B of B⊑A; CR2 under BOTH conjuncts (once when equal); CR3 by B of B⊑∃r.A; CR4 by filler B of ∃r.B⊑A for both triggers; CR6 by sub-role; CR7 by first and by second role — and the dispatcher offers each rule only the matching bucket. On an incoming edge, CR4's companion trigger walks the stored S(Y) and looks each subsumer up as a filler key.\n\nWhy: the full scan made every derived fact cost Θ(|axioms|) rule calls, each allocating a result list that was nearly always empty. OBI (26k axioms) took 172,108 ms to reason; GO never finished.\n\nWhy it is lossless: every rule's first guard is an equality on exactly the key it is filed under, so an axiom in another bucket is one the rule would have rejected. The rule functions, their @examples and structural @posts are unchanged. Enforced three ways: `test-indexed-dispatch-matches-reference` replays every stored fact of 18 fixtures through both the indexed dispatcher and the retained full-scan `apply-el-rules-reference` and requires identical conclusion sets; the goldens captured on the unindexed engine (45 fixture reports, RO and OBI hashes, round counts included) are reproduced byte for byte; and three mutations each turned the suite red — CR2 filed under one conjunct, CR4's on-edge trigger dropped, the filler index keyed by A instead of B.\n\nMeasured (single-threaded, --timings): OBI reason 172,108 → 401 ms; RO 46 → 4 ms; GO end to end 13.4 s (parse 0.9, prepare 7.0, reason 5.5), exit 2 with one omission, 459,329 subsumptions, 12 rounds.\n\nThe module is named `premise`, not `index`: slop-rdf already owns a module `index` (IndexedGraph), and two modules of one name transpile to the same slop_index.c — the first build overwrote the triple store." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7d9facaf-6d1b-4f3f-8cd0-ff223580b686> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
