<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/95f6058d-0d67-49ae-8020-1729e35dfc14> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/95f6058d-0d67-49ae-8020-1729e35dfc14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The CLI's -I takes a file, not a directory" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/95f6058d-0d67-49ae-8020-1729e35dfc14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/95f6058d-0d67-49ae-8020-1729e35dfc14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`howl validate ROOT -I FILE` (repeatable) loads FILE, standardizes its blank nodes apart, reads its owl:Ontology IRI, and adds that IRI to the imports-resolved attestation passed to `classify`. An -I document that declares no ontology IRI is a usage error (exit 3). SPEC §9 amended from `-I DIR`. Decided by the user on recommendation, 2026-09-14.\n\nWhy: -I is the caller's attestation that a document IS a declared import — the trust boundary that turns an unresolved-import omission into coverage. Naming each file makes the attestation explicit; a directory scan attests whatever happens to sit in the directory (stale copies, two files claiming one IRI). Neither SLOP std nor slop-rdf can list a directory, and a `struct dirent` FFI binding differs between macOS and Linux. The first consumer calls the library from Rust with an in-memory attestation (SPEC §15 Q5), so directory convenience only matters for CI, where a shell loop provides it." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/95f6058d-0d67-49ae-8020-1729e35dfc14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/95f6058d-0d67-49ae-8020-1729e35dfc14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-14T22:57:47.956753Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
