<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b25fcbb1-05d6-4f04-bab4-9515b39f67e7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The corpus is converted to Turtle at fetch; only the source hash is pinned" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b25fcbb1-05d6-4f04-bab4-9515b39f67e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b25fcbb1-05d6-4f04-bab4-9515b39f67e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL reads Turtle only (SPEC §6.1's parse · slop-rdf seam), and the pinned OBO corpus is RDF/XML. corpus/fetch.sh verifies each .owl against its MANIFEST sha256, then converts it with rdflib to a sibling .ttl (written aside and renamed, skipped when up to date). MANIFEST.toml pins `converter_rdflib = \"7.6.0\"`, and fetch.sh warns when the installed rdflib differs. The derived .ttl is not hashed. `make corpus-acceptance` runs HOWL over the converted RO and OBI.\n\nWhy only the source: measured 2026-09-14, two rdflib conversions of RO produced different bytes (sha256 prefixes 15aeee95… and f5b04b53…), so a derived hash cannot be pinned; canonical blank-node relabelling (rdflib.compare.to_canonical_graph, then sorted N-Triples) IS deterministic but took 26 s on RO and 33,573 s (9.3 h) on OBI." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b25fcbb1-05d6-4f04-bab4-9515b39f67e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
