<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b25fcbb1-05d6-4f04-bab4-9515b39f67e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/be8d1173-51d6-402d-9b30-0455079e7a15> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Context owns the derived facts; Saturation owns the round's queues" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Per-concept facts live inside the Context that owns them — `(root, subsumers, succs, preds)`. The round's deltas live in `Saturation` as `(queues (Map Node Queue))`, NOT as a field of Context. The global Saturation record holds the context registry, the queues, the `active` frontier, `active-count`, and the iteration count. Cross-context conclusions travel as Addressed messages.\n\nWHY THE QUEUE IS NOT A CONTEXT FIELD. `(Set T)`/`(Map K V)` are pointers in SLOP; `(List T)` is a value struct. Mixing them in one record stored in a Map makes the write-back requirement differ per field with nothing in the type to say so, and the failure is silent under-derivation. Removing the list makes Context UNIFORMLY aliased-by-pointer, so \"a Context read out of the map IS the one in the map\" holds without exception and the write-back question disappears for the type entirely.\n\nIt also unwelds two lifetimes that were conflated: `subsumers`/`succs`/`preds` are the monotone result that survives into `Outcome.saturation`, while a queue is per-round scratch with no business being serialized alongside it. SPEC.md §6.4 already says as much by making the frontier a property of the ROUND (`active := contexts with a non-empty Δₙ₊₁`) rather than of the concept.\n\nTHE OWNERSHIP INVARIANT, restated and strengthened: a worker mutates ONLY the context it currently holds, and during the join phase it mutates NOTHING — every conclusion leaves as a message and is folded in at the barrier. This is what keeps completion rules pure functions from (context, incoming Derived, axiom) to a list of outgoing messages, which is what makes per-rule faithfulness contracts statable at all.\n\n`preds` (incoming role edges) remains non-redundant with `succs`: CR4/CR5 take a premise about Y (B ∈ S(Y)) to a conclusion about X (A ∈ S(X)), so a context learning a new subsumer must notify its predecessors. This is ELK's backward link and why edges are stored twice.\n\n`Saturation` also carries `active-count`, redundant with `active` and earning it: `set-elements` allocates the whole frontier array and is uninterpreted to the WP checker, so testing emptiness through it costs a copy per round AND a proof. An `(Int 0 ..)` is interpreted, which puts the fixpoint test inside Z3's reach.\n\nImplemented and green in howl at 17/17 tests, 23 verified contracts (src/types.slop, src/saturate.slop). SPEC.md §6.2 updated to match." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T04:36:50.341106Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Context owns the derived facts; Saturation owns the round's queues" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/65db656d-afe2-49bc-80aa-0d3677bca2e9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b36adc54-6a36-49c7-bb41-a4744cb6caab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c713b09e-f804-4fba-a01c-8b23e84374c6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c713b09e-f804-4fba-a01c-8b23e84374c6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The canonical report is a line list; the clock lives only in the CLI" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c713b09e-f804-4fba-a01c-8b23e84374c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c713b09e-f804-4fba-a01c-8b23e84374c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A run is compared by one text — `report-lines` (src/report.slop): verdict, termination, round count, inconsistency, then every omission, unsatisfiable class and subsumption in the canonical order extraction and the gate already impose — and that text carries nothing that is not a function of (input, budget). Timings are measured by the CLI with `(now-ms)` around the two library calls `prepare` and `reason` and printed on STDERR; nothing under src/ reads a clock, and `make test` fails if one appears.\n\nWhy: M1 (e) requires byte-identical reports across worker counts and the goldens gate every performance change on exactly these bytes. A duration on stdout makes two correct runs differ; a clock read inside the engine violates the input-determined contract outright. The split `classify` = `prepare` then `reason` is the only honest classification-only measurement boundary from outside the library, and the timed CLI path is literally those two calls, so it cannot drift from the port's path. `rounds` is printed at fixpoint too, because a performance change that alters round count changes what a capped run can see even when the fixpoint answer is identical.\n\nShape details that were forced: a list of lines rather than one string, because `string-concat` copies and GO's ~10^6 subsumption pairs would make report building quadratic; the renderer does NOT re-sort, so a sort dropped upstream shows up as a changed report instead of being papered over; stderr goes through `c-inline` fwrite because SLOP `print` reaches stdout only and an `ffi` binding named `write` resolves to std file's FileMode variant and transpiles to an enum initializer.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §9 (new --report/--max-iterations/--timings paragraph), §6.8; cli/main.slop; src/howl.slop prepare/reason; Makefile no-clock guard. Baseline measured with it: OBI reason_ms 172,108 on the unindexed engine." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c713b09e-f804-4fba-a01c-8b23e84374c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
