<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dcd621be-2202-4ec3-a687-84b2d063cfd1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/eb2b4af4-057e-426a-bc78-69c25d659eab> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e2168bfa-23c3-41f7-8db3-a837a5b1dae1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e2168bfa-23c3-41f7-8db3-a837a5b1dae1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Corpus projections materialize as Turtle, pinned by content including blank-node structure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e2168bfa-23c3-41f7-8db3-a837a5b1dae1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e2168bfa-23c3-41f7-8db3-a837a5b1dae1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`project.py --materialize` writes each entry's v0 projection to corpus/vendor/NAME-VERSION.v0.ttl (not committed), serialized as Turtle by rdflib, and pins it BY CONTENT.\n\n**Content pins.** Each `.removals` header carries three:\n- the ground-triple sha256 (no blank node at either end, canonical as it stands);\n- the blank-node triple count;\n- `projected_bnode_sha256`, a digest of the blank-node part in which each blank node is named by a hash of its own outgoing content, recursively. It is label-free, so stable across parses, and it changes whenever structure changes.\n\n**One check.** `check_graph` compares a parsed file with those pins and requires census to find 0 out of profile. `--materialize`, `--verify` and the corpus differential all run it, so nothing is diffed that is not the pinned projected theory.\n\n**Projection rules:**\n- **Reifications:** a removed axiom's `owl:Axiom` reification goes with it, because HOWL's stage 0 would rebuild the axiom. A reification of an (s, p) that lost a triple is kept only if its target still matches a SURVIVING (s, p, o), structurally for blank nodes.\n- **Chains** are judged against §5.2's range/composition condition on the graph the other removals leave, so a chain is not removed for a range the projection itself deletes.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Rewiring one restriction's owl:onProperty in the materialized OBI kept the ground hash and count, and failed both project-verify and diff-corpus on the blank-node digest.\n- corpus/test_project.py (8 tests, run by materialize, project-verify and CI) covers label-freedom, the rewiring, a reified copy with an extra annotation, a surviving reification, the two-pass chain check, and malformed and inherited-range chains. Each fix was seen red under a mutation." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e2168bfa-23c3-41f7-8db3-a837a5b1dae1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
