<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e613b055-386a-47e2-8748-192cc59dd02d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "External conformance suites check HOWL against answers nobody on the project wrote" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e613b055-386a-47e2-8748-192cc59dd02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e613b055-386a-47e2-8748-192cc59dd02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "corpus/conformance.py runs HOWL against expected answers written outside the project. The sources are pinned by commit and sha256 in corpus/conformance.sha256 (179 files), fetched, and never committed.\n\n**The four suites:**\n- **w3c.** Every Approved EL-profile, Direct-Semantics consistency and inconsistency test of the W3C OWL 2 conformance suite (all.rdf at owlcs/hermit-reasoner 65d38905), checked against HOWL's `inconsistent` line. 39 ok, 26 outside v0.\n- **w3c-entailment.** The suite's positive and negative entailment tests, checked where the conclusion is a named-class SubClassOf/EquivalentClasses. 2 ok, 10 outside v0, and 17 not-expressible (their conclusions are individual types, property axioms or complex expressions, which the report does not state).\n- **elk.** ELK's classification tests (liveontologies/elk-reasoner cc556787). Inputs are converted by the pinned OWL API; the expected taxonomy is closed and compared by entdiff. 33 ok, 32 outside v0, 1 oracle-lossy.\n- **elk-entailment.** ELK's query/entailment tests, checking the named-class subsumptions among the expected (non-)entailments. 3 ok, 5 outside v0, 8 not-expressible.\n\n**Outcomes and the record.** Every outcome is recorded in corpus/conformance-status.txt, and a changed record fails the run. `outside-v0` records carry HOWL's omission kinds and flag `census-clean` when the independent census disagrees. Two lines are flagged, both gate-only refusals: an unresolved import and non-regular chains. `oracle-lossy` marks input the OWL API cannot convert faithfully. A mismatch is never recorded.\n\n**Defects found in HOWL, each now a hazard fixture, a src/test.slop test and a golden, and each seen red under a mutation:**\n1. **A false coherent** (DisjointClasses-002). Undeclared individuals named only by class assertions got no context.\n2. **A needless inconclusive** (WebOnt-Restriction-001). `rdf:type` over a blank-node class expression was not read as a class assertion.\n3. **A needless inconclusive** (AnnotationAnnotations-001). `owl:Annotation` nodes were decoded, not consumed.\n\n**Why:** the capability probes carry expectations HOWL's implementer wrote, and the differential compares with oracles run live. Neither tests the assumptions the fixtures share with the code." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
