<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f2ad5629-149e-43eb-a620-10aed5cc57f0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/fcaacd9d-661c-4372-aff4-89dc89f80684> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The oracle is a pinned Java program on one OWL API, not ROBOT" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "oracle/ is a Gradle project around one class, howl.oracle.Main. It runs ELK 0.6.0 (io.github.liveontologies) and HermiT 1.4.5.519 on OWL API 5.1.20, which is forced with `strictly` because HermiT's POM asks for 5.1.9. It runs on a JDK 21 toolchain.\n\n**Pins.**\n- Versions live once, in build.gradle.kts.\n- The dependency closure is locked in gradle.lockfile, and strict sha256 verification is in gradle/verification-metadata.xml. Tampering with one hash fails the build.\n- The wrapper pins Gradle 9.7.1 by distributionSha256Sum.\n- At startup the program checks each jar's MANIFEST Implementation-Version against the pins, and aborts on a mismatch.\n- It does NOT check getReasonerVersion(), because HermiT 1.4.5.519 reports 1.4.1.513 there.\n- It refuses to run on any JDK but 21. build/oracle launches the toolchain JVM, because installDist's script would take whatever `java` is on PATH.\n\n**Fail, don't diff.**\n- A file fails, and gets no report, when the loader metadata shows any unparsed triple or guessed declaration.\n- It also fails when anything logs WARN or higher. A logback appender records the warnings, HermiT's Configuration.warningMonitor feeds the same record, and commons-logging reaches it through jcl-over-slf4j.\n- Anything on the process's stderr fails the harness.\n- ELK's capture is proven live by a tripwire: out-of-profile/allvalues.ttl must make ELK warn both before the first file and after the last, so a per-JVM dedup of warnings can't hide one." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
