<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/55edf275-dd54-42fb-98c9-7b2938ed6bd6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/fca77e04-870b-4ee2-9416-5a39f76db57b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/146f2a05-1428-4777-b9d7-182a2e816b72> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/2c40fcd0-ef98-4bb0-bfb3-b44d549cbbde> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL saturation state is context-owned, not global maps" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Per-concept facts live inside the Context that owns them (root, subsumers, succs, preds, queue); the global Saturation record holds only the context registry, the `active` frontier, and the iteration count. Cross-context conclusions travel as Addressed messages.\n\nWhy: SPEC.md §6.2 originally described one global record of S(·)/R(·) maps while §6.6 described ELK-style per-context saturation with propagation messages. Those are different architectures and nothing reconciled them — this resolves it in favour of the context model, because §6.6's parallelism claim (GROWL's fork-join machinery transfers almost unchanged, with the context as shard key) is only true if contexts own their state. Global maps would make every rule firing a write to shared state, which is exactly what the decomposition exists to avoid.\n\nThe ownership invariant: a worker mutates ONLY the context it currently holds; every conclusion about a different concept leaves as a message. This makes completion rules pure functions from (context, incoming Derived, axiom) to a list of outgoing messages, which is also what makes the per-rule faithfulness contracts statable.\n\n`preds` (incoming role edges) is not redundant with `succs`: CR4/CR5 take a premise about Y (B ∈ S(Y)) to a conclusion about X (A ∈ S(X)), so a context learning a new subsumer must notify its predecessors. This is ELK's backward link, and it is why edges are stored twice.\n\nRejected alternative: keep global concurrent S(·)/R(·) maps and shard only the work queue — rejected because it contends on every derivation and does not match the ELK decomposition the performance envelope is borrowed from.\n\nConsequence: nominals become expensive rather than merely deferred — an individual is reachable from many contexts and can force them to merge, breaking context independence. That is why nominals are the one deferred v0 construct that could change the data model rather than extend it. Captured 2026-08-10." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ff60d323-bdc6-4e9a-ae99-acb6e214e62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T23:08:47.369275Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
