<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The OWL API has blind spots, so some inputs can't be diffed against any oracle" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Both oracles and `oracle convert` load input through the OWL API. Two shapes load as a different theory, or not at all:\n\n1. **Repeated operands where OWL 2 reads operands pairwise by position** (`AllDisjointClasses`/`AllDisjointProperties`/`AllDifferent` members, `distinctMembers`, `disjointUnionOf`, and functional-syntax DisjointClasses and similar). The OWL API stores them as a set and drops the repeat with no warning and no unparsed triple, so `(A B A)` loses \"A is empty\". HermiT then answers \"A satisfiable\" (ELK's DisjointSelf test).\n2. **An annotation on an ontology annotation** (`owl:Annotation`). The OWL API's RDF parser leaves its triples unparsed.\n\ncorpus/differential.py (`owlapi_blind_spots`, which compares operands structurally) excludes such input from every oracle comparison. corpus/conformance.py records such tests as `oracle-lossy`. The unparsed-triple refusal is not weakened. HOWL's own answer on each shape is pinned instead: hazards/disjoint-repeated-member.ttl (A unsatisfiable) and hazards/annotated-annotation.ttl, each with a golden, an acceptance line and a src/test.slop test." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T03:01:37.541493Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The OWL API has blind spots, so some inputs can't be diffed against any oracle" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3349619e-fe38-4cd3-b1f0-461a2e085d4c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb5178bb-b322-4505-9acf-4f4da1c33015> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/39de5a2d-f88b-4ead-815a-b7e172eeb3fa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/39de5a2d-f88b-4ead-815a-b7e172eeb3fa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL's output stage must be designed as returnable DATA, not 'write a file' — the consumer needs canonically ordered subsumptions back across the FFI, and Turtle emission is one serialization of that result rather than the result itself." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
