<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/39de5a2d-f88b-4ead-815a-b7e172eeb3fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/39de5a2d-f88b-4ead-815a-b7e172eeb3fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:29:04.952619Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/39de5a2d-f88b-4ead-815a-b7e172eeb3fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL's output stage must be designed as returnable DATA, not 'write a file' — the consumer needs canonically ordered subsumptions back across the FFI, and Turtle emission is one serialization of that result rather than the result itself." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f19adcf-2201-4823-9e5b-08dd02cf85e4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f19adcf-2201-4823-9e5b-08dd02cf85e4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "missing-declaration-cmp compares the `referring` lists element-wise and therefore ASSUMES both are already sorted, which is the field invariant types.slop states. Every construction site must honour it; comparing two unsorted lists element-wise is not an order at all." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
