<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Census now enforces the range/composition condition and reads data sub-properties" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Reconciling census with HOWL's gate on the materialized corpus (M1 slice 4) found three things the independent census had missed. Each was fixed in census, never by deriving removals from HOWL's gate:\n\n1. **RO: 48 property chains break SPEC §5.2's range/composition condition** (a range imposed on the chain's super-role that its last role does not share). census.py now implements the condition from the SPEC (`inadmissible_chains`: told sub-property closure, `owl:equivalentProperty` both ways, structural class-expression equality). Its 48 match HOWL's refusals exactly.\n2. **OBI: one data-property `rdfs:subPropertyOf`** had been counted as `SubObjectPropertyOf`.\n3. **RO: three of those chains were also reified,** and the projection kept their `owl:Axiom` nodes, from which HOWL's stage 0 rebuilt the chains. project.py now removes a removed axiom's reification with it.\n\n**Result:**\n- RO removes 390 axioms / 1,644 triples (was 342 / 1,361); OBI removes 385 / 5,849 (was 384 / 5,848).\n- HOWL reads every materialized entry with omitted 0 (`make corpus-acceptance`).\n- Reverting fix 2 makes `project-verify` fail, and was seen to." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T04:58:07.94288Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Census now enforces the range/composition condition and reads data sub-properties" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3f867247-4d7b-46c2-bbfd-0c89eadced9e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1b29794-7999-4d7d-9ec3-9ab0c63967e7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/430f1dda-868a-4168-ae0f-a343300284db> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/430f1dda-868a-4168-ae0f-a343300284db> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Queue list order is bucket order and is not content-canonical, so it must never escape into a report. It does not, because `classify.extract-findings` is the only path out — which makes that function's canonical ordering a determinism obligation rather than a tidiness one." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
