<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/63b3abb0-b1cc-4056-9889-ab04794a0e3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T04:37:40.558096Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/63b3abb0-b1cc-4056-9889-ab04794a0e3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Initialization must commit Δ₀ into the store as well as queueing it, because in this design initialization IS the barrier preceding round 0 — making SPEC.md §6.3 step 4's 'empty subsumers set' a statement about S₋₁ rather than about the state the driver first sees." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6419c384-39ee-4c61-a8f1-65f4257a0b27> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6419c384-39ee-4c61-a8f1-65f4257a0b27> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "census.py counts the three `_:b owl:inverseOf` defining triples as InverseObjectProperties and the enclosing chain/inclusion as in-v0, so HOWL and the census agree on the out-of-profile COUNT for the inverse fixture for different reasons; the census's classification of inverse operands is owed a fix." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
