<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL v0 language: ranges by elimination, nominals out, four dispositions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/00683550-a89a-4865-8633-222f7600d5e6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5cecf538-1be2-4f57-a979-888812c3b7d4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL v0 accepts exactly ELH⊥R+ plus domain and range axioms, plus ABox assertions. Ranges are handled by the PUBLISHED ELIMINATION CONSTRUCTION during normalization — never by a new completion rule. The rule set is exactly CR1–CR7 from the cited CEL formulation.\n\nRANGES: IN, BY ELIMINATION. A construct census over the first consumer's corpus found 90 rdfs:range uses, and the honest bounded stub HOWL replaces already decides domain/range coherence, so shipping without ranges would be a functional regression at the swap. Domain needs no new machinery — domain(r) ⊑ C is just ∃r.⊤ ⊑ C, handled by CR4. Range uses the X_{r,D} rewrite from \"Pushing the EL Envelope FURTHER\" (the OWLED paper; the 2005 paper defines EL++ WITHOUT ranges): after ordinary normalization and after chain decomposition, for each normal-form GCI C ⊑ ∃r.D introduce X_{r,D} and replace it with C ⊑ ∃r.X_{r,D}, X_{r,D} ⊑ D, and X_{r,D} ⊑ A for every A in ran_T(r), where ran_T is computed over the TOLD role hierarchy so r inherits every super-role's range. X_{r,D} is SHARED per (r,D) pair. Complex range fillers are normalized to a name first, via an intermediate form that still carries ranges — so NormAxiom needs no range constructor.\n\nTwo things the published rewrite does not give you. It touches existential GCIs only, so ASSERTED EDGES need HOWL's own extension: installing r(a,b) must also seed every A in ran_T(r) into S(individual(b)). And its admissibility condition — every range imposed on a composed role t must also be imposed on the chain's last role, the same class expression, through the told hierarchy on BOTH sides — is a precondition of the construction, which is why it lives in the gate rather than in rule code.\n\nNOMINALS: OUT. The same census found zero ObjectHasValue and no nominal use (only inert owl:NamedIndividual declarations). Nominals were the one deferred construct that would have changed the DATA MODEL rather than extended it, because an individual is reachable from many contexts and would break context independence.\n\nFOUR DISJOINT DISPOSITIONS, and the matrix is a total function over RawAxiom. In-profile (classified) · Inert (annotation vocabulary — IGNORED, contributes and costs nothing) · Consumed (declaration triples — produce no NormAxiom but ARE read, supplying entity typing and populating the input signature) · Out-of-profile (enumerated in the report, verdict inconclusive). Consumed is a PREPROCESSING disposition settled before the gate, not a fourth gate branch; collapsing it into Inert loses declarations and with them every declared-but-unused class.\n\nThe two failure modes are opposite and both silent: a permissive decoder drops an unsupported LOGICAL axiom and returns a false coherent, while a conservative one marks ANNOTATION axioms out-of-profile and returns false inconclusive on every documented ontology. Inertness is therefore STRUCTURAL, not an IRI whitelist — any decoded AnnotationAssertion whose property is a declared annotation property is inert. The matrix should be GENERATED from the RawAxiom union so exhaustiveness is a compile-time property; a construct absent from it is a spec bug, not an implementer's judgement call.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §5.2 (the exact v0 language, the elimination block, the disposition tables), §6.3 (normalization), §6.4 (\"Ranges add no rule\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
