<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL v0 language: ranges by elimination, nominals out, four dispositions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL v0 language: ranges in, nominals out, inert vocabulary carved out" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL v0 accepts exactly ELH⊥R+ plus domain and range axioms, plus ABox assertions encoded as concept names. Everything else is enumerated as out-of-profile; annotation vocabulary and declaration triples are INERT (silently dropped), not out-of-profile.\n\nWhy ranges are in: a construct census over the first consumer's corpus found 90 rdfs:range uses, and the honest bounded stub HOWL replaces already decides domain/range coherence. Shipping without ranges would be a functional regression at the swap. Domain needs no new machinery (domain(r) ⊑ C is just ∃r.⊤ ⊑ C, handled by CR4); range is a genuine calculus extension requiring a new rule (CR8: (X,Y) ∈ R(r), range(r) ⊑ A ⟹ A ∈ S(Y)) that fires in the successor's context. Baader et al.'s revised EL++ covers range restrictions but imposes a syntactic interaction constraint against role composition — that constraint is part of the language definition and is enforced at the gate, not in the rule code.\n\nWhy nominals are out: the same census found zero ObjectHasValue and no nominal use (only inert owl:NamedIndividual declarations). Nominals were the one deferred construct that would have changed the data model rather than extended it, because an individual is reachable from many contexts and can force them to merge — breaking the context independence the parallelism rests on. Answered no for this consumer.\n\nWhy the inert category is load-bearing: every real ontology is annotation-heavy. A gate with only two categories (in-profile / out-of-profile) returns inconclusive on everything and the reasoner is useless. Three disjoint categories are required, and the inert set must be an explicit enumerated whitelist rather than a permissive default — a permissive default silently drops logical axioms, which is the fail-silent hazard the whole out-of-profile discipline exists to close.\n\nDatatype properties (34 uses in the census) stay out: the consumer partitions them and keeps a told-coherence side-check rather than HOWL growing a concrete domain. Keeping the language honest is worth more than absorbing one more construct.\n\nCoverage consequence: 33 owl:inverseOf uses remain out-of-profile until v1 Horn-SHIQ, so v0 buys instance-bearing verdicts and range coherence, not a clean pass on the consumer's own theory. Captured 2026-08-10." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
