<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-11T00:27:50.633709Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL v0 language: ranges in, nominals out, inert vocabulary carved out" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8c9b3db7-cf31-4932-b9ba-5f9c36593e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/793f66a9-f643-4a36-a4c1-dd2d1a6c34ce> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A gate may not be more permissive than the proof it cites" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL's profile gate must admit exactly the ontologies covered by the published completeness proof for its calculus. Deviation in either direction requires its own proof; the permissive direction silently forfeits the completeness claim.\n\nThe instance: HOWL v0 needs the OWL 2 EL global restriction on property chains and ranges. The published condition requires the range imposed on a composed role t to ALSO be imposed on the last role s of the chain — the same class expression, reachable through the told role hierarchy. A draft instead derived a weaker condition from first principles: allow range(s) = D for any D with told D ⊑ C, reasoning that a node satisfying D satisfies C anyway.\n\nThat reasoning may even be sound. It was still wrong to adopt, for a reason that has nothing to do with whether the semantics work out: HOWL's completeness rests entirely on implementing a calculus someone has PROVED complete (the verification posture is that Z3 checks faithfulness to the calculus, while soundness and completeness come from the published proofs). A gate admitting ontologies outside the proved condition leaves the proof behind, and the citation no longer covers what the engine does. Wanting the relaxation later is legitimate; it needs a proof, not a citation.\n\nCompounding error worth remembering: the draft carried the instruction \"if the published condition turns out to be weaker, relax the gate to match; never the reverse.\" That assumed the derived condition was the stricter one. It was the looser one, so following the instruction would have locked in a permanently over-permissive gate — the guidance pointed at the dangerous direction while sounding cautious. When writing a to-verify note, do not assume which side of the published condition your draft sits on; state that either direction needs justification.\n\nGeneral rule: for any gate, admissibility condition, or precondition justified by citation, the cited source defines the boundary. Derivation may explain the boundary but may not move it. Captured 2026-08-12." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-13T05:21:53.448217Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae25e3d4-de8a-437c-ab8e-47692cfb5b6b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A gate may not be more permissive than the proof it cites" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL distinguishes inconsistent, unsatisfiable, and incoherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Three separately-defined conditions, not synonyms:\n\n  inconsistent  := ⊥ ∈ S(⊤)  or  ∃ individual a. ⊥ ∈ S(individual(a))\n\n  unsatisfiable := ∅                                        when inconsistent\n                   { iri | class-node(iri) ∈ input signature,   otherwise\n                           iri ≠ owl:Nothing,\n                           ⊥ ∈ S(class-node(iri)) }\n\n  incoherent    := inconsistent ∨ unsatisfiable ≠ ∅\n\nWhy it matters: the flagship service is COHERENCE validation, and coherence is the WEAKEST of the three — an ontology with an unsatisfiable named class is incoherent whether or not it is inconsistent. Conflating them either under-reports (missing the unsatisfiable class that is the whole point) or over-reports.\n\nUNDER INCONSISTENCY THE SET IS EMPTY BECAUSE IT IS UNDEFINED. An inconsistent ontology has no model, so every class is unsatisfiable — yet raw ⊥ ∈ S(A) finds none of them when the inconsistency arrived through an individual context, since C(a) with C ⊑ ⊥ leaves every class context untouched. Reporting the raw set would be a lower bound so misleading it is worse than nothing: `inconsistent: true` with `unsatisfiable: []` reads as \"consistent classes\". It therefore follows `subsumptions` — empty and documented as undefined-because-inconsistent, with differential tests skipping unsatisfiable-set comparison for inconsistent inputs. `incoherent` is unaffected, since `inconsistent` alone already makes it true.\n\nTHE owl:Nothing TRAP. Initialization seeds Δ₀(N) = {N, ⊤} for every node, so ⊥ ∈ S(⊥) holds BY CONSTRUCTION as soon as owl:Nothing appears — which any disjointness axiom guarantees. Without excluding owl:Nothing, `unsatisfiable` is non-empty for essentially every real ontology, `incoherent` is always true, and `howl validate` exits 1 universally. That is a FALSE FAIL, the mirror of the false-pass class the spec spends most of its effort on — less dangerous, because uselessly noisy surfaces on first use where dangerously quiet does not, but still a bug. A construction-guaranteed fact is true without being a finding. Individual and fresh contexts are excluded for the same reason: a fresh node is a normalization artifact with no input counterpart, and an unsatisfiable individual context IS the inconsistency case the first definition already carries.\n\nINTERFACE CONSEQUENCE, DELIBERATE. `howl validate` exits 1 on INCOHERENT, because a CLI gate has one bit to spend and should spend it on the weaker, more useful condition. The port's `TBoxReport.consistent` stays `!inconsistent`, with unsatisfiable classes in their own field, because that consumer distinguishes them downstream — so `consistent: true` alongside a non-empty `unsatisfiable_classes` is a valid consistent-but-incoherent report there, and a failing condition for the consumer. The two surfaces differ on purpose; both are documented as such.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §6.2 (the three definitions and the undefined-because-inconsistent paragraph), §6.4, §8.4, §9, §10 items 14 and 15." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:57:20.019117Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL distinguishes inconsistent, unsatisfiable, and incoherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Differential oracles must be capability-probed per construct" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/17beb51b-607b-4ff3-99de-b2afbb9dc801> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A reference reasoner counts as an oracle only for the constructs it is PROVEN to process, verified by probe at harness startup. An oracle that fails a construct's probe is not an oracle for that construct, and comparisons involving it are routed elsewhere.\n\nThe concrete exposure: ELK describes itself as implementing A FRAGMENT OF OWL 2 EL, and object-property ranges have historically been outside it — while v0 admits ranges. Run against an ELK that silently ignores a range axiom and a correct range-derived subsumption is reported as a HOWL EXTRA: a false fail in the acceptance suite, blamed on the implementation rather than the oracle. The unconditional \"any ontology HOWL accepts, ELK accepts\" of an earlier draft is not something this spec can assert about someone else's release, and it is load-bearing enough that an implementer trusting it would certify HOWL against an oracle that processed a different theory.\n\nRequired harness discipline:\n- Pin exact ELK and HermiT versions in the repo, alongside the corpus pins.\n- Capability-probe every v0 construct against each oracle at startup — one fixture per construct whose expected entailment the oracle must produce.\n- Fail the harness on any oracle warning or ignored-axiom diagnostic rather than diffing through it.\n- Route range-bearing cases to a confirmed-complete reasoner (HermiT, or ELK only if the pinned version passes the range probe); range-bearing fixtures are mandatory at M1, not avoided.\n\nTwo comparison rules travel with it. Compare the ENTAILMENT PREDICATE `entails-sub(A,B)`, not serialized taxonomies — HOWL's taxonomy is deliberately bottom-compressed, so diffing it against an oracle's entailment closure reports a mismatch on every corpus entry with an unsatisfiable class, a correct implementation failing its own acceptance test for representational reasons. And compare over ALL ordered pairs of named input classes for acceptance: a \"fixed probe set\" that is any proper subset lets a reasoner omit every entailment outside it and still be certified complete. Sampled probe sets are for production cross-checks only.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §10 item 1 (differential testing), §5.2 (the ELK-oracle paragraph), §12 M1 acceptance (b)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:26:57.517816Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b293cf6e-d681-41a0-a895-fbe9eb20d4b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Differential oracles must be capability-probed per construct" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL: only a complete run may report coherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3eacfa8e-800e-452f-9547-e4ee85c2f45d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A HOWL reasoning run must carry a RunStatus (complete | out-of-profile | resource-limit | cancelled), and only `complete` licenses a coherence verdict, a complete hierarchy, or a minimal repair.\n\nWhy: HOWL's flagship service is `validate` as a CI gate. Three separate paths reach a non-fixpoint state — a profile too weak for the ontology, the max-iterations cap, and cancellation — and in the original SPEC all three exited as if the check had passed. That is the unsafe failure direction: a validator that silently returns \"coherent\" when it could not actually tell is worse than no validator, because CI trains users to trust it.\n\nMechanics: partial results remain SOUND (every rule is faithful), so a derived ⊥ ∈ S(C) is real whatever the status; it is the ABSENCE of a fact that carries no information. Hence a partial run may report the unsatisfiable classes it found, but never coherence. Surfaces as CLI exit code 2 (inconclusive), distinct from 0 (coherent) and 1 (incoherent). `--strict` controls only whether HOWL refuses to run vs. returns a marked-partial result — no flag can promote an incomplete run to a verdict.\n\nRejected alternatives: (a) warn-by-default on out-of-profile constructs with --strict opt-in (the original SPEC design) — rejected because the default failure direction is a silent false pass and safety must not be opt-in; (b) treating a hit iteration cap as an ordinary loop exit as GROWL's engine-run does — rejected because a capped run and a coherent ontology are indistinguishable at the Saturation level.\n\nConsequences: every entry point returns an Outcome (status + saturation), never a bare Saturation; CI must treat exit 0 alone as pass; direct-subsumer reduction and minimal repair are meaningful only on a complete outcome, since a hitting set over an incomplete justification set is not minimal.\n\nNote: before v2 (CB SROIQ) there is no complete fallback rung to escalate to, so out-of-profile input has nowhere to go but inconclusive. Captured 2026-08-10 from an external review of SPEC.md." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T23:03:43.846366Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL: only a complete run may report coherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bb86deca-2b68-476a-8878-c825d9964e50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/65db656d-afe2-49bc-80aa-0d3677bca2e9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL distinguishes inconsistent, unsatisfiable, and incoherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Three separately-defined conditions, not synonyms:\n\n  inconsistent  := ⊥ ∈ S(⊤) or ∃ individual a. ⊥ ∈ S(individual(a))\n  unsatisfiable := { iri | class-node(iri) is a context, iri occurs in the INPUT,\n                           iri ≠ owl:Nothing, ⊥ ∈ S(class-node(iri)) }\n  incoherent    := inconsistent ∨ unsatisfiable ≠ ∅\n\nWhy it matters: HOWL's flagship service is COHERENCE validation, and coherence is the weakest of the three — an ontology with an unsatisfiable named class is incoherent whether or not it is inconsistent. A draft defined only `inconsistent` and let the verdict rule speak vaguely of \"any contradiction derived\", which under-reports exactly the case the tool exists to catch.\n\nThe owl:Nothing trap: initialization seeds Δ₀(N) = {N, ⊤} for every node, so ⊥ ∈ S(⊥) holds BY CONSTRUCTION as soon as owl:Nothing appears — which any disjointness axiom guarantees. Without excluding owl:Nothing from `unsatisfiable`, the set is non-empty for essentially every real ontology, `incoherent` is always true, and `howl validate` returns exit 1 universally. That is a FALSE FAIL, the mirror of the false-pass class this spec spends most of its effort on. It is less dangerous (uselessly noisy rather than dangerously quiet, so it surfaces on first use) but it is still a bug, and worth noting that a construction-guaranteed fact is true without being a finding. Fresh and individual contexts are excluded for the same reason: a fresh node has no input counterpart, and an unsatisfiable individual context IS the inconsistency case.\n\nInterface consequence, deliberate: `howl validate` exits 1 on INCOHERENT, because a CLI gate has one bit to spend and should spend it on the weaker, more useful condition. The MOOSE port's TBoxReport.consistent stays `!inconsistent`, with unsatisfiable classes in their own field, because that consumer distinguishes them downstream — so `consistent: true` alongside a non-empty unsatisfiable_classes is a coherent thing for HOWL to report there. The two surfaces differ on purpose; both are documented as such. Captured 2026-08-12." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-13T05:58:21.055782Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL distinguishes inconsistent, unsatisfiable, and incoherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c7023d3a-4a30-4a92-a859-b1dcbb5819ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/b0e575c2-5fbb-4c9b-ae27-b17b7f9ab42d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Expressivity is claimed construct-by-construct, never by label" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3eacfa8e-800e-452f-9547-e4ee85c2f45d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL never claims coverage by naming a logic. Capability is stated construct-by-construct, and every registration, flag and document phrase must match what the calculus actually implements.\n\nThe instances, which are the same error at three surfaces:\n- `profile()` must register v0 as `BoundedDl(ProfileDecl { name: \"howl-el-v0/ELH⊥R+ ...\" })`, NOT as `ElPlusPlus`. Registering the label would be the overclaim committed in code, inside a system whose entire posture is anti-overclaim; `ElPlusPlus` is reserved for an engine actually complete for EL++.\n- \"an OWL 2 DL reasoner\" is reserved for v2 and is NOT earned by a SROIQ(D) calculus alone. OWL 2 DL is the OWL 2 structural language satisfying its global restrictions under Direct Semantics; it closely corresponds to and extends SROIQ, which by itself provides neither datatypes nor punning. An earlier draft's \"OWL 2 DL is SROIQ(D)\" would let a future implementer treat a conventional SROIQ(D) calculus as sufficient without checking the construct surface or the global restrictions.\n- The v2 CLI flag is `--profile sroiq`, not `dl`, because the rung is the SROIQ OBJECT fragment and a flag named `dl` would promise OWL 2 DL.\n- The gap from v0 to EL++ is the complete enumerated list (nominals, concrete domains, ObjectHasSelf, reflexive role inclusions, the two built-in object properties) — describing it as \"just nominals and concrete domains\", as earlier drafts did, overclaims coverage.\n\nWhy this earns constraint status rather than being style: the \"DL reasoner\" label is earned by being complete for a NAMED logic, so \"complete for roughly EL++\" earns nothing and a label that outruns the calculus makes a false completeness claim reachable by anyone reading the registration instead of the spec.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §3.2 (Terminology discipline), §5.2 (the subset claim and its enumerated gap), §8.4 (\"profile() must not overclaim\"), §9 (flag naming), §14." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f8ee2abd-6704-40c6-91ca-9be70cb8f4f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:26:49.672774Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
