<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0165b8ad-6735-4c1b-b8dc-970c9bc1b612> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f15852f8-c7e1-4d93-a347-d915de5e041e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Profile the real corpus before fixing guessed hotspots" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The M1 slice-1 plan listed front-end quadratics found by READING the code — a doubled gate call, a list-scan dedup in signature-nodes, linear fresh-name lookups, a per-axiom range scan. All were real and all got fixed, and GO still did not leave the front end: 4 minutes in at 11.8 GB. One 5-second `sample` of the running process named the actual blocker, which was on nobody's list: `stage0-header` tested each of 1.4M triples' subjects against the ontology-node and axiom-node LISTS with `term-eq`, and GO reifies 131,783 axioms. Replacing the scans with a `(Set Term)` let GO finish in 13.4 s end to end.\n\nWhy the reading missed it: the helper was named `term-in-set-of` and documented \"membership over a small term list\", which is true of every fixture; and OBI, the largest corpus entry run until then, has no `owl:Axiom` reification in its Turtle at all, so the cost was invisible on everything that had been measured.\n\nRule: before optimizing, run the REAL input under a sampler and fix the top frame; treat code-reading candidates as hypotheses to confirm, not as the work list. And when a corpus entry is added, check which input shapes it exercises that earlier entries did not — a shape absent from every measured input hides its cost completely." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-15T02:49:02.877593Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
