<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/14e5fd5a-19d1-40cf-8997-bc43d1575dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7d9facaf-6d1b-4f3f-8cd0-ff223580b686> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The slop verify boundary, as of 0.2.3 with #168 and #172" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "What `slop verify` can prove about HOWL's rules is set by how the verifier models a body, not by what the claim means. Re-probed on slop 0.2.3 plus slop-lang/slop PRs #168 and #172 (#166, #170), 2026-09. Supersedes the 0.2.1 record.\n\nNOW PROVABLE:\n1. Quantified claims over a LOOP-FREE push-built result. A body `(let ((mut r (list-new …))) … r)`, with pushes only inside do/let/when/if/cond/match, is modelled exactly as a sequence. So `forall`, `exists` and `list-contains` over `$result` are proved or refuted. On 0.2.3 alone the soundness direction came back unknown and completeness FAILED, because `list-push` was an opaque call and `_seq_push` had never been wired in.\n2. `match` in a contract binds every payload at its declared sort (#166). Before, only the first name was bound, and later names read another arm's payload, which let false contracts verify.\n3. A callee's `@post` and `@property` are assumed at a call, guarded by the path and the callee's `@pre`.\n\nSTILL NOT:\n4. A result built in a LOOP. The exact model doesn't follow loops, so a quantified claim over it is unknown. HOWL's four loop rules stay owed.\n5. Opaque predicates. `node-eq`, `role-eq` and `set-has` are uninterpreted. Equal inputs aren't known to give equal answers, and `node-eq(b,a1) ∧ node-eq(b,a2)` doesn't give `a1 = a2`. So a contract states premises with the body's own calls, and a self-join's second side states the body's case split.\n6. Timeouts are an honest outcome. Some true contracts don't decide in reasonable time; CR2's completeness as one disjunction didn't decide even at 120 s. Restating it as the body's own split made it decide in the normal timeout. A false claim often comes back unknown (timeout) rather than failed. That's sound, since it is never verified.\n7. `record-new`/`union-new` inside a contract is a fresh value that nothing equals. Write completeness as `exists` over field equalities.\n8. The transpiler lowers a multi-payload `match` in expression position wrongly (#171), which breaks a `SLOP_DEBUG` build of such a `@post`. State those facts as `@property`, which is verify-only.\n\nTHE METHOD:\n- Probe with minimal pairs, and mutate the body to see a proved property go red.\n- Before citing an upstream issue as a blocker, check its current state. #69 had been closed three weeks earlier, and the user caught the stale citation.\n- The fix then exposed a deeper gap that the closed issue didn't cover.\n- Every Codex review round of the verifier change found real false-verification paths, eleven across six rounds (two on #168, four on #172). Several were already wrong on main: tail record fields under a shadowing `let`, quoted enum arms, `Float` payloads." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
