<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The slop verify boundary, as of 0.2.3 with #168 and #172" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bcf088-7d14-4136-8c29-8790b8a793e7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1d0011c7-4851-4d51-b36a-aa240eb619b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/772eff39-94f7-4692-92ea-23f39da47e50> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A context registry keyed on declarations drops undeclared individuals" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Contexts come from `signature-nodes`, which reads declared classes and declared individuals plus the endpoints of asserted edges. NAMED-INDIVIDUAL DECLARATIONS ARE OPTIONAL in OWL 2. So an individual that appears only in class assertions (`:stewie a :Boy , :Girl`, with Boy and Girl disjoint) got no context: its GCI individual(stewie) ⊑ Boy hung off a node no rule ever visited. Coverage read complete, and HOWL reported COHERENT on an INCONSISTENT ontology, a false coherent with omitted 0.\n\nThe class-assertion case in normalize.slop even says \"so the individual gets a context\". But a GCI doesn't create a context; only `signature-nodes` does. Every hand-written fixture declared its individuals, so nothing caught it. The W3C OWL 2 conformance test DisjointClasses-002 caught it on the first run of corpus/conformance.py.\n\nFix: NormOutput.asserted records each class-assertion subject, and `signature-nodes` gives it a context, as it already did for edge endpoints. Regression fixture: hazards/undeclared-individual.ttl, which must report inconsistent, exit 1. No golden moved, and RO/OBI/GO report hashes are unchanged.\n\nA second, sound gap surfaced in the same run. An `rdf:type` with a blank-node class expression (`:a a [∃op.⊥]`) fell through to `unrecognized`, so HOWL answered INCONCLUSIVE where the answer was INCONSISTENT (WebOnt-Restriction-001). Fixed in decode.slop and census.py alike. Regression fixture: hazards/anonymous-class-assertion.ttl.\n\nRule: every node an axiom can mention must get a context from the same place that normalizes the axiom, not from a separate signature scan that assumes declarations. And fixtures written by the implementer share the implementer's assumptions, so external conformance suites (W3C, ELK) are how those assumptions get tested." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T02:25:01.155232Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A context registry keyed on declarations drops undeclared individuals" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5cecf538-1be2-4f57-a979-888812c3b7d4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e613b055-386a-47e2-8748-192cc59dd02d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/22ac762c-e623-4d2d-9ce8-5f0364110510> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f2ad5629-149e-43eb-a620-10aed5cc57f0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SLOP list-push invents an arena member when none is in scope" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`(list-push (. s field) v)` inside a function with NO `arena` binding in scope lowers to `slop_arena_alloc(s.arena, …)` — the transpiler synthesizes an `arena` member on the list's base type rather than reporting that it has no arena to allocate from. The failure surfaces in `cc` as \"no member named 'arena' in 'struct X'\", not as a checker error.\n\nWith an arena in scope the same expression lowers correctly, which is why `saturate.slop`'s `seed-node` has always compiled while an otherwise identical helper does not.\n\nVERIFIED BY ISOLATION, and the first diagnosis was wrong. The initial reading was \"list-push into a record FIELD does not compile, because the arena is derived from the base expression\" — and a workaround was written into HOWL's source on that basis, copying the field to a local before pushing. A second probe that differed ONLY in taking an `arena` parameter compiled and ran correctly, which falsified it: the base being a field is irrelevant, the absent arena binding is the whole cause. The workaround and its comment were removed rather than left standing, because a comment asserting a false toolchain limitation is worse than no comment — the next reader propagates it.\n\nPRACTICAL RULE FOR HOWL: any function that mutates a container takes `Arena` explicitly and carries `@alloc arena`. That is already forced for `set-put` / `map-put` / `set-elements`, which emit the bare identifier `arena`; `list-push` belongs in the same class and its failure mode is worse because it reaches the C compiler instead of the checker.\n\nUpstream issue owed against slop: the missing diagnostic, not the lowering.\n\nGENERAL RULE: when a toolchain bug is diagnosed from one failing case, construct the minimal variant that isolates the suspected cause before writing the explanation into source. A plausible-but-wrong mechanism embedded in a comment outlives the bug." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T18:35:48.89342Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/277488f7-ebb2-4785-8618-26a60f727a79> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "SLOP list-push invents an arena member when none is in scope" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Route a correction to supersede, not to a fresh Lesson" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When a design position changes, superseding the record that asserts the old position is the operation. Minting a NEW record about the correction feels like discharging the obligation — it is a real write, it is true, it is useful — but it retracts nothing, so the stale assertion stays `accepted` and stays in recall.\n\nMeasured on HOWL's own graph at spec approval (2026-08-17), after fourteen review rounds:\n\n| Kind | Records | Drifted |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lesson | 10 | 0 |\n| Constraint | 4 | 3 |\n| ArchitecturalDecision | 2 | 0 |\n| Requirement | 1 | 0 |\n\nEvery correction HAD been captured — as a Lesson. The Lesson layer was a complete and accurate record of the whole review; the Constraint layer was a set of snapshots frozen at the moment each was written. The three drifts:\n- A Constraint specified range support as a new completion rule CR8. The spec later removed CR8 (it would have claimed completeness from a proof not covering the implemented calculus) and captured the governing principle as a NEW Constraint, \"A gate may not be more permissive than the proof it cites\" — two days later, while the record asserting CR8 stayed accepted. The graph held the correct rule and the wrong instance simultaneously.\n- A Constraint required \"a RunStatus (complete | out-of-profile | resource-limit | cancelled)\" union. The spec replaced it with three independent axes, and the correction went into Lesson \"Reasoner status is three independent axes, not one status union\" rather than into the Constraint.\n- A Constraint's definition of `unsatisfiable` never gained the `∅ when inconsistent` case the spec added.\n\nWHY THE KIND PREDICTS DURABILITY. A Lesson is append-only by nature — \"we made this mistake, here is why\" stays true however the design moves. A Constraint or ArchitecturalDecision asserts a CURRENT position, so it perishes when the position changes. Capturing one mid-review, while the position is still being argued, is what makes it stale; the only Constraint that survived clean was the one written last.\n\nTWO PRACTICES THAT FOLLOW.\n1. Before writing a Lesson about a correction, ask which existing record the correction FALSIFIES. If one exists, supersede it — the Lesson is then optional colour, not the fix.\n2. Prefer capturing a still-moving decision as a Lesson (durable) over a Constraint (perishable) until the design settles, and mint the Constraint at approval.\n\nDETECTION. Recall truncates long descriptions at roughly 2000 characters, so comparing a spec against recall output verifies the opening of each record and nothing else — all three drifts here were in truncated tails. A real drift audit needs full descriptions via `sparql`, scoped to Constraints and ArchitecturalDecisions, since Lessons do not perish." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:59:37.816955Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Route a correction to supersede, not to a fresh Lesson" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/29204dfe-0826-425d-ae17-d4ed733edaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/59735b43-50e4-423f-be01-b484357f726d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Z3/WP contracts prove faithfulness, never semantic soundness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A weakest-precondition checker reasons about program states, so it can prove a rule implements the calculus it claims to. It cannot quantify over models, so it can never prove a conclusion is ENTAILED. The dividing line for contract design is structural vs. model-theoretic — not soundness vs. completeness.\n\nThe gotcha: SPEC.md originally carried a per-rule @post of `subsumers-superset $result.subsumers sat.subsumers` under a comment claiming \"every S(X) entry added is entailed by the premises.\" That postcondition is pure monotonicity — it says the result grew — and says nothing whatever about the new entries. The §7 table then banked a \"Z3-reachable: Yes\" row on it. Same error for normalization: conservative extension is model-theoretic and is not an ordinary structural postcondition.\n\nThe fix: state FAITHFULNESS instead — every conclusion emitted is licensed by that rule's premises holding in the input state, quantified over the emitted list. Semantic soundness is then faithfulness (Z3) PLUS the calculus's published soundness proof (Baader et al. for CEL), exactly parallel to how completeness was already handled. The honest phrase is \"verified faithful to a proven calculus\", not \"verified sound\".\n\nSecond-order gotcha found while writing the replacement: a premise the function does not itself establish (e.g. CR4's B ∈ S(Y), which the driver guarantees by only delivering b to that context) belongs in a @pre, not a @post. Asserting it in the postcondition reproduces the original error — claiming something the body never establishes.\n\nOpen dependency: this assumes SLOP's @post supports forall/exists over the emitted list. If the contract language is quantifier-free the contracts cannot be stated as written and the \"Yes — structural\" rows overclaim again; fallback is a per-conclusion witness naming the premises fired on, which is checkable quantifier-free. Captured 2026-08-10." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T23:09:09.04501Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2acb7b52-67ea-4f9d-a7b3-242e6811dd10> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Z3/WP contracts prove faithfulness, never semantic soundness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A seed written only to Δ₀ is invisible to round 0's rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "In HOWL's barrier-synchronized driver, initialization must write a derived fact to BOTH the context store and the round-0 queue. Writing only the queue is silent, total, and produces a false COHERENT.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. The driver commits Δₙ into the store at the END of round n−1, so during round n the store IS the frozen snapshot Sₙ. Initialization is that barrier: nothing commits Δ₀, because Δ₀ is defined to be already in S₀. A fact placed only in the queue therefore arrives as a MESSAGE that rules can react to, while S(target) never contains it — so any rule needing that fact as a PREMISE rather than as a trigger cannot fire.\n\nTHE INSTANCE. `deliver-seed` installed asserted role edges and their inherited range facts into Δ₀ only. The mandatory identity fixture — Disjoint(C,D), range(r)=C, range(s)=D, r(a,b), s(c,b) — then reported COHERENT. Both ranges reached individual(b) as messages, neither entered S(b), so CR2 could never find the OTHER conjunct of `C ⊓ D ⊑ ⊥`, and the disjointness never fired. Coverage was empty and the verdict was clean: a wrong answer with no symptom at any interface.\n\nWHAT MADE IT HARD TO SEE. Every upstream stage was correct and independently tested: the seeds were produced (a passing test asserted both C and D on individual(b)), the contexts existed, the normal form contained `sub-and C D ⊥`. The failure was entirely in the handoff, and the only observable was the final verdict. Bisecting by inspecting S(b) directly — rather than re-reading the producing code — is what located it in one step.\n\nTHE PRECEDENT WAS ALREADY IN THE FILE. `seed-node` documents the identical hazard from the opposite direction: omitting the STORE write leaves S(N) empty through round 0, so CR2 cannot find a conjunct and CR4 cannot satisfy B ∈ S(Y) against a seed. Any new initialization path has to satisfy the same obligation, and `round-commit` is the shape to copy — it writes the store and the queue together for every Derived variant.\n\nGENERAL RULE: in a semi-naive driver where the store is the committed snapshot, \"deliver a fact\" always means two writes. A single-write delivery compiles, type-checks, runs, and silently weakens the engine." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T18:35:32.738562Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A seed written only to Δ₀ is invisible to round 0's rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/3405b30d-b1b9-4c21-9580-a230223b436c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f15852f8-c7e1-4d93-a347-d915de5e041e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The slop verify boundary: expression shape, not claim meaning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "What `slop verify` can discharge is decided by how an expression is SHAPED, not by what the claim means. The boundary is documented nowhere upstream and every rule below was established by controlled probe — minimal pairs differing in one construct.\n\n1. `or` AND `and` IN A FUNCTION BODY MAKE THE RETURN VALUE OPAQUE. Identical `@post` over the same boolean record field: `(or (. r b) (> (. r n) 0))` fails with a counterexample; `(if (. r b) true (> (. r n) 0))` verifies. The boolean FIELD is fine — the boolean OPERATOR is the blocker. Reach for `if` before concluding something is unverifiable.\n\n2. `@property` QUANTIFYING OVER A PUSH-BUILT `$result` FAILS, AND POISONS SIBLING `@post`s. `(@property p (forall (m $result) (== (. m to) root)))` over a list built with `list-push` does not go unknown — it fails, and adding it makes a previously-passing `@post` on the same function fail. This is the one that misleads, because the natural diagnosis is that the @post was wrong. GROWL's rule-faithfulness properties survive only by coming back UNKNOWN, which is not a failure. Consequence: per-rule faithfulness pairs are currently unstatable in this checker and belong in OWED plus fixtures.\n\n3. A LOOP ANYWHERE IN THE BODY MAKES `$result` OPAQUE. Hoist the loop into a helper and keep the contracted function branch-only.\n\n4. AN `if` BETWEEN TWO `record-new`s LOSES FIELD PROJECTION — even when both arms trivially satisfy the claim. Only a single unconditional `record-new` keeps `(. $result f)` visible. Per-field `if`s inside one `record-new` do not rescue it either.\n\n5. TWO EXCLUSIVE BRANCHES THAT EACH PUSH DEFEAT A LENGTH BOUND. `<= 1` fails with a two-element counterexample because the checker assumes both fire. Set a flag in either branch and push ONCE: same semantics, and it proves.\n\n6. NO INTERPROCEDURAL REASONING. A callee is uninterpreted (`fn_outcome-is-complete_1=[else -> True]`). Where a safety property must cross a call, add a REDUNDANT local check; where it must cross a loop, `@loop-invariant` carries it — HOWL proves `iteration <= max-iterations` that way despite every call in the loop being opaque.\n\n7. `const` values are opaque; `set-elements` and `list-get` are uninterpreted, but `(Int 0 ..)` FIELDS are interpreted — which is why an explicit `active-count` puts the fixpoint test inside Z3's reach where `(list-len (set-elements ...))` cannot.\n\n8. PREFER A TYPE OVER A CONTRACT. `emit-edge` takes a `LogicalEdge` and returns an `EdgePair`, so \"both halves exist\" is enforced by construction and each destination is a provable field access; as a two-element list it needed `list-get` and was only testable.\n\nTHE METHOD, which is the durable part: do not diagnose a prover limitation from a single failing example. Every one of these came from a minimal pair, and three earlier \"not reasonably verifiable\" verdicts were overturned that way. When a contract fails, suspect the SHAPE of the body before the truth of the claim — and when adding one contract breaks another, suspect interference before either.\n\nMapped on HOWL 2026-08-19; 23 verified contracts, 0 failing." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T04:38:34.000424Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The slop verify boundary: expression shape, not claim meaning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/772eff39-94f7-4692-92ea-23f39da47e50> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/351e4c85-8221-400b-ad97-ffc72f8d83ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/85e6f9fb-40ea-497b-b689-3074f1a4ad52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
