<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Validity checks need false-fail suites, not just false-pass suites" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Any gate, admissibility condition, or rejection rule needs tests asserting what it ACCEPTS, not only what it rejects. Reviewing exclusively for \"does this let something bad through\" leaves the opposite failure — refusing valid input — systematically unexamined.\n\nEvidence from HOWL's review history: four consecutive rounds found only false-pass defects (silent incompleteness, dropped axioms, unverifiable obligations). A pass deliberately aimed at false-fails then found four in one round, all in text that had already been reviewed several times:\n- ⊥ ∈ S(⊥) holds by construction from the initialization seeds, so without excluding owl:Nothing from the unsatisfiable set every ontology with a disjointness axiom reports itself incoherent and validate exits 1 universally.\n- A generic cycle detector over role inclusions rejects equivalent simple roles (r ⊑ s, s ⊑ r) and transitivity (r ∘ r ⊑ r), both of which OWL regularity expressly permits — a witness policy that was wrong in the accepting direction while looking rigorous.\n- A declared-but-unused class got no context, so the reasoner silently did not know it existed.\n- A test plan asked for a \"coherent-but-inconsistent\" fixture, which the definitions make impossible — an unsatisfiable specification, not just an untested one.\n\nWhy these hide: false-passes are what safety review is trained on, and a rejection rule reads as conservative and therefore safe. But over-rejection has its own severity ladder — refusing a user's correct ontology is a product failure, and a gate that rejects too much also invalidates any completeness claim conditioned on it.\n\nPractice adopted: for every rejection rule, write the accepting cases that sit closest to the boundary — especially cases that LOOK like violations under a naive implementation. HOWL's RBox test item now has explicit \"rejects\" and \"accepts\" halves for exactly this reason. Also: check that each test fixture is satisfiable against the definitions before writing the test. Captured 2026-08-12." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-13T06:11:02.332937Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3bd2b34-5079-46b3-9c67-63798ea80b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Validity checks need false-fail suites, not just false-pass suites" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A missing union arm is a SLOP warning; -Werror=switch makes it an error" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SPEC.md §5.2 requires the OWL disposition matrix to be \"a total function over `RawAxiom` ... generated from it rather than maintained by hand\", so that exhaustiveness becomes a compile-time property instead of a proofreading exercise. The obvious way to discharge that is a `match` with no catch-all arm. **SLOP's own type checker only WARNS on a non-exhaustive match** — `warning: non-exhaustive match on Colour: missing blue` — and the build succeeds. Relying on it as stated would have left the guarantee imaginary.\n\nWhat the transpiler actually emits is better than it first looks, and it is what makes the fix available. The generated C is a `switch` over the tag with `SLOP_UNREACHABLE()` placed AFTER the switch rather than as a `default:` arm — and the runtime header says why in a comment (csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h:86-88): \"so -Wswitch still fires on a missing enum case\". `SLOP_UNREACHABLE()` itself prints to stderr and `abort()`s, so the runtime behaviour is fail-loud rather than a silently wrong disposition. That matters: a missing arm returning tag 0 would have made an unhandled out-of-profile construct decode as in-profile, i.e. a false coherent.\n\nSo the guarantee is obtained one layer down: **`-Werror=switch` in the C build**. A missing variant then fails the build and names it exactly — `error: enumeration value 'exh_Colour_blue' not handled in switch`. Verified against the whole existing tree first: HOWL was already exhaustive everywhere, so adopting it cost nothing and locks the property in for every `match` in the codebase, not just the disposition matrix.\n\nThe general lesson: when a plan says \"X will be a compile-time guarantee\", check which compiler is supposed to enforce it before building on it. Here the SLOP checker and the C compiler disagreed about severity, and the enforcement lived in the one nobody had thought to ask.\n\nEvidence: probe in scratchpad (deliberately omitted union arm); Makefile CFLAGS now carry `-Werror=switch` with the rationale inline; csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h:86-93." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-22T20:49:14.818482Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f933de6e-50a6-4cbe-95e1-20fe897a8e0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A missing union arm is a SLOP warning; -Werror=switch makes it an error" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Check OWL 2 profile membership against the W3C grammar, not memory" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "OWL 2 EL includes SameIndividual, DifferentIndividuals, NegativeObjectPropertyAssertion, NegativeDataPropertyAssertion, HasKey, the data-property axioms and DataSomeValuesFrom/DataHasValue — a README row written from memory listed the first five as \"outside OWL 2 EL\".\n\nPattern: the constructs v0 rejects for its own reasons (no nominals → no equality, no negation) are easy to misfile as rejected by the profile too. That error understated the distance between v0 and OWL 2 EL in exactly the direction the expressivity-by-construct constraint warns about (\"everything else v0 rejects, OWL 2 EL rejects too\" was false). SPEC §5.2's \"complete omitted list\" (the gap sentence near line 411) carries the same undercount for the profile.\n\nRule: any \"in / not in OWL 2 EL\" cell is checked against the productions in W3C OWL 2 Profiles §2.2 (ClassExpression, ObjectPropertyAxiom, DataPropertyAxiom, Assertion, HasKey) before it is written. The profile's own not-supported list is: ObjectAllValuesFrom/DataAllValuesFrom, all cardinalities, ObjectUnionOf/DisjointUnion/DataUnionOf, ObjectComplementOf, multi-member ObjectOneOf/DataOneOf, DisjointObject/DataProperties, Irreflexive/Symmetric/Asymmetric, InverseObjectProperties, Functional/InverseFunctional object properties — plus anonymous individuals (Individual := NamedIndividual)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-14T05:27:02.746286Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe1ea93a-da21-483e-9cb1-4582452949fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Check OWL 2 profile membership against the W3C grammar, not memory" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Goldens captured on the pre-change engine gate every performance change" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Before any performance work touches the engine, capture canonical reports from the UNCHANGED binary — every fixture as committed text, large corpus entries (RO, OBI) as report hashes, each ending in its exit code — and require every later change to reproduce them byte for byte, round counts included (`make golden`; `make golden-update HOWL=<binary>` for deliberate changes only). Keep a copy of the pre-change binary outside build/ so the baseline can be recaptured honestly after the tree has moved on.\n\nWhy: a faster engine that derives one subsumption fewer, or needs one more round, is a correctness regression that no fixture exit code notices. Round count is part of the report because it determines what a capped run can see. Serves the Constraint \"Reports are input-determined\" (007e982c) and the benchmark Constraint (11c160af): speed may never be bought with a different report.\n\nThe gate must itself be proven non-vacuous. The first capture passed `--report` before the input file; the CLI refused it, and every golden recorded that usage error with exit 3 — a gate the old and the new engine would both pass forever. It was caught only by cross-checking the corpus golden hashes against an independent baseline run, which disagreed. So both targets now reject any output that does not begin with the report header, and a capture is accepted only after an independent run reproduces its hash.\n\nApplied in M1 slice 1: goldens captured on the unindexed engine; two independent baseline runs of RO and OBI agree byte for byte; the premise-index engine reproduces all 45 fixture reports and both corpus hashes." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-15T02:44:27.718613Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e1699f76-c4d6-4602-9b1c-574e2c3ba506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Goldens captured on the pre-change engine gate every performance change" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: HOWL v0 language: ranges by elimination, nominals out, four dispositions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record specified range support as a NEW COMPLETION RULE — \"CR8: (X,Y) ∈ R(r), range(r) ⊑ A ⟹ A ∈ S(Y), that fires in the successor's context\". SPEC.md now rejects exactly that. CR8 was derived from first principles: plausible, possibly even correct, but the published extension of EL++ with range restrictions establishes tractability and completeness BY ELIMINATING RANGES THROUGH FRESH CONCEPTS, not by adding that rule. Shipping CR8 would have meant claiming completeness from a proof that does not cover the calculus actually implemented — the same failure the accepted Constraint \"A gate may not be more permissive than the proof it cites\" records, committed at the rule level instead of the gate level. The rule set therefore stays at CR1–CR7, all of which are in the cited CEL formulation.\n\nTwo further corrections travel with it. The construction is in \"Pushing the EL Envelope FURTHER\" (the later OWLED paper), not the 2005 \"Pushing the EL Envelope\", which defines EL++ without range restrictions — citing the wrong one leaves an implementer reconstructing the transformation from scratch. And the disposition taxonomy is now FOUR categories, not three: Consumed (declaration triples) is a preprocessing disposition settled before the gate runs, and collapsing it into Inert loses declared-but-unused classes, which M0 explicitly requires." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:29:41.635644Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/00915473-732c-4d39-a347-a4f0e41a2ecb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: HOWL v0 language: ranges by elimination, nominals out, four dispositions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: The slop verify boundary, as of 0.2.3 with #168 and #172" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The 0.2.1 record said per-rule faithfulness pairs were unstatable because slop#69 made a quantified @property over a push-built result fail. #69 was closed (PR #126) three weeks before S2 planning cited it as a blocker; the user caught the stale citation. Re-probing 0.2.3 showed the real gap was deeper: soundness came back unknown and completeness failed because list-push was never modelled. slop PRs #168 (match binds every payload at its declared sort) and #172 (exact model of a loop-free push-built result) close it, and HOWL's seven loop-free rules now prove both directions. Rows 2 (#69) and 4 (if between record-news) of the old record are superseded; the loop, opaque-predicate and timeout boundaries remain." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-26T18:27:22.70179Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/164520bc-6657-4b0c-a94c-418f3d2061f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: The slop verify boundary, as of 0.2.3 with #168 and #172" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: The slop verify/test boundary, as of 0.2.1" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Re-probed against slop 0.2.1 rather than assumed from release notes, and two of the record's rules changed status while two survived — so the record as written would send a reader to the wrong workaround in both directions.\n\nRETIRED. `@example` is now a working substitute for the blocked `@property` faithfulness contracts, and under 0.1.2 it was actively harmful: examples with non-scalar arguments were skipped AND counted as passes (#71). The superseded record told readers the contracts were unstatable and did not say that the obvious fallback silently reported success. HOWL now has six executing, mutation-tested rule examples where it had six fake-green ones.\n\nSTILL TRUE, confirmed by re-running the minimal pairs, not by reading the issue tracker: `@property` over a push-built `$result` still fails and still poisons a sibling `@post` (#69, open), and an `if` between two `record-new`s still loses field projection (#70, open). Both were verified failing on 0.2.1 before this record was written — the issues being open was treated as a hypothesis, not as evidence.\n\nAlso folded in: the list-literal trap in example expectations, which fails confusingly enough to cost a debugging cycle, and the fact that the syntax valid in ordinary code is precisely the one that breaks there." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-22T02:34:26.763729Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1902593f-83e2-4983-a722-a7fff009f112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: The slop verify/test boundary, as of 0.2.1" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Corpus projections materialize as Turtle, pinned by content including blank-node structure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A Codex review showed that the ground hash plus the blank-node count do not pin blank-node structure: rewiring a restriction's owl:onProperty keeps both. On OBI that was seen to pass. The corpus differential checked even less (the ground hash only). Two latent projection defects were also found: a reification that differs from its removed axiom survived, and chains were judged against ranges the projection itself removes." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T05:59:11.630583Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1fa94d5a-ea5c-447b-be33-dc7f77b2dcf1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Corpus projections materialize as Turtle, pinned by content including blank-node structure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Check what the generator emits before keying a Set on a type" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's concrete claim is fixed: slop 0.2.1 emits correct multi-field equality for multi-payload union variants (slop-lang/slop#66, closed), verified here by direct test — inserting `(pair A B)` no longer makes `set-has (pair A C)` true, and the set size comes back 2 rather than 1.\n\nLeft standing, the record forbids something that is now safe, and a prohibition that has quietly expired is worse than none: the next reader either obeys it needlessly or discovers it is stale and stops trusting the neighbouring warnings too.\n\nWhat survives is the method, and it is the part worth keeping: before using a type whose equality is GENERATED as a hash key, read what the generator actually emits for it. The failure mode was not a crash but a plausible wrong answer — silent under-derivation, invisible to any fixture with a single filler per role — and it was found by reading the transpiler rather than by testing, because no test would have been written for a case nobody suspected.\n\nAlso worth recording: HOWL never depended on the bug being absent. The round delta is keyed on `Node`/`RoleId`, which was chosen defensively but turns out to be the shape the commit-at-barrier design wants anyway — the delta mirrors `Context` field-for-field and commit is three parallel loops with no translation. Nothing had to be reverted on the upgrade, which is the argument for defensive shapes that are also good shapes." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-22T02:33:31.989685Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2126a382-6db4-4ba9-b98e-86fc8f963903> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Check what the generator emits before keying a Set on a type" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Seed the delta — and the round-0 snapshot, which is not the same thing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's guidance — titled \"Seed the delta, NOT the store\", and prescribing \"S₋₁ := ∅ with Δ₀(N) := { derived-sub(N), derived-sub(⊤) }\" — reads as forbidding the store write. Implementing the driver showed that reading is wrong, and wrong in a way that costs exactly the entailment the project exists to derive.\n\nIts core claim stands and is untouched: seeds written ONLY into the store leave every queue empty, so `active` is empty at round 0 and the driver reports `fixpoint` before firing a rule. What it missed is the other half. §6.4 defines the round-0 snapshot as S₀ = S₋₁ ∪ Δ₀ = Δ₀, so the seeds must ALSO be visible in the store by the time round 0 joins. In a driver that commits Δ at the preceding barrier, initialization IS that barrier.\n\nFollowing the old record literally — queue only, store empty — produces the mirror failure: S(N) stays empty throughout round 0, so CR2 can never find the other conjunct of a `sub-and` and CR4 can never satisfy B ∈ S(Y) against a seed. Confirmed by mutation on the real implementation: removing the two store writes makes the §3.1 litmus fail and nothing else, so `Mother ⊑ Parent` is lost and the engine silently reverts to a materializer while every other test stays green.\n\nThe generalisable point is why one record could carry both errors: \"empty store, seeds in the delta\" conflates S₋₁ (genuinely empty) with the state the driver first READS (which is S₀ = Δ₀). Those are different states, and a rule stated about the wrong one fails in whichever direction the implementer happens to read it." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T04:38:05.822324Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/439b81e8-3ef6-4942-9474-f90d1fc0c49d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Seed the delta — and the round-0 snapshot, which is not the same thing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: The slop verify boundary: expression shape, not claim meaning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's findings all hold; implementing CR1–CR7 and extraction found four MORE boundary rules, one of which inverts the record's implicit advice.\n\nThe record treated `@property (forall (m $result) …)` as an available tool — it is the shape SPEC.md §6.4 and GROWL both use for rule faithfulness. On a list built with `list-push` it is not merely unavailable: it FAILS with a counterexample, and its presence makes any `@post` on the same function fail too. That last part is the surprise, and it cost real time: three rule contracts that passed in isolation went red on adding a property, and the natural diagnosis is that the @post was wrong. A controlled probe (q1 @post alone → verified; q2 @property alone → failed; q3 both → the @post fails) isolated it. GROWL's equivalents survive only because they come back UNKNOWN, which is not a failure.\n\nThree further rules, all found the same way: a loop anywhere in a body makes `$result` opaque; an `if` between two `record-new`s loses field projection even when both arms are visibly empty; and two exclusive branches that each `list-push` defeat a `<= 1` bound that a single push behind a flag proves.\n\nNet effect on HOWL: 13 → 23 verified contracts. Two obligations moved to OWED with the reason stated in-source rather than left as failing contracts, because a red `make verify` destroys the signal from every contract that does hold." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T04:38:34.000424Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/698ea7ee-ecf1-408c-b1fb-fc9cf9e92274> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: The slop verify boundary: expression shape, not claim meaning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: The Z3 contract boundary in SLOP is or/and in the body" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's headline finding was wrong. It claimed \"BOOL RECORD FIELDS are opaque — `(. f inconsistent)` yields a counterexample every time\", generalising from a failing case without isolating the variable. A controlled probe — two functions with an IDENTICAL contract over the same boolean record field, differing only in body — shows the field is not the problem: `(or (. r b) (> (. r n) 0))` fails with a counterexample, `(if (. r b) true (> (. r n) 0))` verifies. The blocker is `or`/`and` IN THE BODY making the return value opaque.\n\nTwo further claims in it were also wrong, and both were \"unverifiable\" conclusions that a five-minute probe overturned. It said the saturate budget bound was unreachable because it needs a loop invariant — `@loop-invariant` exists, and the bound verifies with it even though both calls inside the loop are uninterpreted. And it treated `list-get` being uninterpreted as the end of the matter for emit-edge's destinations, when returning a RECORD instead of a two-element list makes the same property a provable field access.\n\nCorrecting these took HOWL from 11 verified contracts to 13, and converted an invariant that was merely tested into one enforced by a type. The generalisable error is diagnosing a limitation from a single failing example rather than isolating the variable: three separate \"not reasonably verifiable\" verdicts were all wrong, and all three were reachable by changing the shape of the code rather than the claim." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-19T18:00:41.744248Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c1b63cb-e98b-4139-bb7d-32e9560c3f08> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: The Z3 contract boundary in SLOP is or/and in the body" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: The slop verify boundary, as of 0.2.3 with #168 and #172" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The first replacement kept only the rows that changed and silently dropped rows of the 0.2.1 record that are still true (or/and opacity, the single-push length bound, no interprocedural reasoning outside the exact model, const/set-elements opacity, the @example splat trap, #66/#67 fixed). Superseding removes the old record from current recall, so those facts would have vanished. This version merges both." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-26T18:27:46.509566Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/6c8c210f-80f6-4373-8ed7-238a29908fd8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: The slop verify boundary, as of 0.2.3 with #168 and #172" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Only a complete run may report coherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record required \"a RunStatus (complete | out-of-profile | resource-limit | cancelled)\" — a single exclusive union. SPEC.md §6.2 rejects that shape outright: coverage, termination and findings are THREE INDEPENDENT AXES, because a run can be both out-of-profile (the input carried axioms outside the fragment) AND resource-limited (the in-profile subset still blew the cap), and a union forces the report to lie about one of them. Cancellation is not a termination variant at all — it leaves the result type entirely as a Fault, because a cancelled partial state is timing-dependent and must be unrepresentable as a result rather than merely discouraged.\n\nLesson 6a81666b (\"Reasoner status is three independent axes, not one status union\") recorded that correction on 2026-08-11, and this Constraint was left asserting the superseded model — the correction was captured in the append-only kind while the record making the stale claim stayed accepted and in recall.\n\nThe record's core claim survives unchanged and is strengthened: only a complete run may report coherent. What changes is the mechanism that establishes completeness — a conjunction over two independent axes rather than a status tag — and the discovery that the union also produced a verdict rule which DISCARDED SOUND RESULTS, since sending every out-of-profile run to inconclusive ignores that inference is monotone." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:56:58.129987Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/727523b8-7bf5-4699-a70a-79e144305c98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Only a complete run may report coherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Context owns the derived facts; Saturation owns the round's queues" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record listed `queue` as a Context field — \"(root, subsumers, succs, preds, queue)\". Implementing the driver showed that shape is a silent-failure trap in SLOP, and the record would lead the next implementer straight into it.\n\nIn SLOP, `(Set T)` and `(Map K V)` compile to `slop_map*` POINTERS while `(List T)` compiles to a VALUE STRUCT {len, cap, data}. For a record stored in a `(Map Node Context)`, that means `set-put` reached through a `map-get` copy is visible in the map, and `list-push` through the SAME copy is not — it updates only the copy's `len`, and where `cap` allows it writes into the shared buffer past the stored length. So four fields need no write-back and one does, nothing in the type says which, the two calls are one keystroke apart, and the failure mode is a silently dropped conclusion.\n\nThe core claim of the record — per-concept facts live in the context that owns them, there are no global S(·)/R(·) maps, cross-context conclusions travel as Addressed messages, and `preds` is not redundant — survives entirely and is unchanged. Only the field list moves, and the ownership invariant is strengthened by it: with the queue gone a worker holding a context writes it NEVER during the join phase.\n\nAlso corrected: `isMotivatedBy` pointed at Constraint/bb86deca, which has itself been superseded by Constraint/65db656d (\"Only a complete run may report coherent\"). The replacement points at the current record." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T04:36:50.341106Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a01921cc-15b7-40e2-922a-f67a60a9dec2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Context owns the derived facts; Saturation owns the round's queues" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Range-bearing inputs gate only on HermiT; ELK's range results are informational" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's consequence said census cannot see owl:AllDisjointClasses. The probe label check added after the Codex review caught this, and census now counts it as DisjointClasses. Routing also gained a guard that the superseded record lacked: input that sits in an OWL API blind spot is not diffed against either oracle." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T03:01:22.035441Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d610f69d-12fa-4e06-801b-05b3c4efa76f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Range-bearing inputs gate only on HermiT; ELK's range results are informational" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: External conformance suites check HOWL against answers nobody on the project wrote" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The inventory was completed at the user's direction (\"know every place HOWL fails, then plan\"). Two entailment suites were added. A third defect (nested annotations) was found and fixed. The OWL API blind spots were found and guarded. The superseded record named the nested-annotation gap as open and covered only two suites." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-27T03:01:21.917745Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e073f515-2524-4d4b-b065-602c0a7d0bf9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: External conformance suites check HOWL against answers nobody on the project wrote" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: HOWL distinguishes inconsistent, unsatisfiable, and incoherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's definition of `unsatisfiable` had no inconsistency case — it read the raw set { iri | ... ⊥ ∈ S(class-node(iri)) } unconditionally. SPEC.md §6.2 now makes the set ∅ WHEN INCONSISTENT, and the reason is substantive rather than editorial: an inconsistent ontology has no model, so under Direct Semantics EVERY class is unsatisfiable, yet raw ⊥ ∈ S(A) finds none of them when the inconsistency arrived through an individual context (C(a) with C ⊑ ⊥ leaves every class context untouched). Reporting that set would be a lower bound so misleading it is worse than nothing: `inconsistent: true` alongside `unsatisfiable: []` reads as \"consistent classes\". The set is therefore empty because it is UNDEFINED, not because nothing is unsatisfiable, and differential tests skip unsatisfiable-set comparison for inconsistent inputs.\n\nAlso sharpened: membership is in the INPUT SIGNATURE, which is the defined term (the signature, not the axiom set, is what \"occurs in the input\" means everywhere in the spec) — the superseded wording said \"is a context, occurs in the INPUT\", which is ambiguous between the signature and the document, and those differ elsewhere: `Findings.subsumptions` is projected over classes in the input DOCUMENT precisely because the signature is pre-populated with built-ins." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:57:20.019117Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e7874ebf-5816-4f42-ac03-5fcd126c25ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: HOWL distinguishes inconsistent, unsatisfiable, and incoherent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Defined-class subsumption through existential restrictions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL must compute subsumptions that are entailed only THROUGH an existential restriction on the defining side — the class of entailment forward-chaining materialization cannot see by construction. This is simultaneously the reason the project exists and the v0 acceptance criterion.\n\nThe litmus (SPEC.md §3.1):\n\n    Parent ≡ Person ⊓ ∃hasChild.Person\n    Mother ⊑ Person ⊓ ∃hasChild.Person\n    ⟹ Mother ⊑ Parent ?\n\nIt is entailed, and it is derivable only through the existential. If HOWL derives it, it is a DL reasoner; if it cannot, it is still a materialization engine. GROWL cannot — OWL 2 RL/DLP is engineered precisely to sidestep the decision problems, so it can neither introduce existential successors nor compute class-level subsumption through them.\n\nWhy it is stated as a requirement rather than a test case: it is the discriminating criterion for the whole design, and it constrains implementation choices that look unrelated. Normalization's polarity rule is the sharpest instance — `Person ⊓ ∃hasChild.Person ⊑ Parent` puts the existential in NEGATIVE position, so it needs `∃hasChild.Person ⊑ X` (a sub-some-lhs) before `Person ⊓ X ⊑ Parent` is in normal form. A one-sided \"definitional\" rewrite emitting only `X ⊑ ∃hasChild.Person` is conservative, incomplete, and fails this exact test while appearing to follow the spec's own example.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §2 (Motivation), §3.1 (the litmus test, also the v0 acceptance criterion), §6.3 step 3 (polarity), §12 M1 acceptance (a)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:24:00.850672Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/49b913bc-f305-4d05-b16f-53f09dc533b2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Defined-class subsumption through existential restrictions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HOWL's execution trigger fired via MOOSE, not the Trivyn pipeline" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL is the unbuilt EL engine behind MOOSE's Living Ontology TBoxReasoner port, and that consumer — not Trivyn's generation or alignment stages — is what v0 is designed against. The plan-on-the-shelf posture in SPEC.md §13 no longer holds.\n\nWhy this trigger outranks the three originally listed: the cost of not building is being paid continuously by a shipped system rather than deferred until a pipeline stage matures. Two ceilings are stub-gated and removable by no other means — (1) instance-bearing candidate deltas cannot reach a Pass, because the honest bounded stub reports every assertion-bearing delta as inconclusive, restricting the whole promotion path to annotation-only changes; (2) dual-engine attestation cannot exist, because the agreement stage needs a second real engine to cross-check against.\n\nDesign consequences already applied to SPEC.md: the port, not the CLI, is the deliverable (FFI from day one, input as a copied in-memory triple buffer, never a store handle); the library path always runs non-strict, since out-of-profile is a report rather than a refusal and a detected inconsistency Fails even alongside out-of-profile axioms (monotone finding beats incomplete coverage); v0 registers as BoundedDl(ProfileDecl) rather than ElPlusPlus, because claiming the latter while implementing a strict subset would commit the overclaim error in code.\n\nKnown integration blocker on the critical path: the consumer's agreement stage currently hard-codes a non-stub ElPlusPlus engine to Inconclusive(EngineUnavailable), because per-probe comparison needs entailment access the report shape does not expose. Plugging HOWL in naively therefore makes that stage fail closed — the engine lands and the pipeline gets less usable. Resolving it needs the inferred hierarchy, or its restriction to a probe set, returned as canonically ordered data across the FFI. Not independently fixable from either side.\n\nAlso reframes the GROWL relationship: the agreement stage cross-checks the EL and RL engines on a deterministic probe set in the EL ∩ RL entailment overlap, where disagreement is an engine fault never resolved by preferring one engine. So HOWL and GROWL are not only composed one-directionally through RDF — they are independent oracles checked against each other in production, making differential testing a live mechanism and agreement with GROWL a standing correctness obligation. Captured 2026-08-10." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-11T00:41:49.534429Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/53e71ad6-2ef7-41b3-8d53-cad39c0a363b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "HOWL's execution trigger fired via MOOSE, not the Trivyn pipeline" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Minimal mapping repair for ontology alignment" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL must check the coherence of a merged theory `O₁ ∪ O₂ ∪ mappings` and return the COMPLETE, canonically ordered family of inclusion-minimal repairs — not one repair, and not a minimum-cardinality repair.\n\nWhy alignment is the stronger case for a complete reasoner than generation QA: alignment COMBINES ontologies, which is precisely when latent incoherence surfaces. BFO/CCO's heavy disjointness axioms are what give the reasoner teeth here. Precedent: LogMap is built around an embedded reasoner doing exactly this (justification/MUPS computation plus hitting set).\n\nWhy the full family rather than one repair: returning one hides the steward's actual choice, and minimum-cardinality silently prefers removing a single high-value mapping over two trivial ones. Only MAPPINGS are removable — axioms from either source ontology are fixed, since repairing a source is a different operation with different consent. Ordering is by cardinality then lexicographically by sorted AxiomRefs, which makes ties deterministic without inventing a confidence metric HOWL has no basis to supply; a consumer with mapping confidences ranks the returned set itself.\n\nThe search needs its own coverage and termination axes, exactly as classification does — `complete` is the conjunction of all four phases (justification enumeration, hitting-set enumeration, candidate verification, and every classification used to establish repairhood or minimality). A hitting set over an incomplete justification set is not a repair at all: it need not hit a conflict that was never enumerated.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §2 (Motivation, \"the stronger case\"), §9 (`howl align-check --repair`), §12 M4 and its \"what minimal means\" block, §10 test 18." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:24:01.338038Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/6005e658-0b6f-40f4-aa1e-2a8fafc0dcf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Minimal mapping repair for ontology alignment" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Coherence validation inside an authoring/CI loop" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "HOWL v0's deliverable is fast semantic coherence validation: decide whether an ontology is consistent, surface EVERY unsatisfiable class, and return the answer in a time that fits an authoring/CI edit loop. Classification is the mechanism; validation is the point.\n\nWhy the EL family is chosen rather than assumed: EL++ subsumption is PTIME, so there is no exponential blow-up to tame; the consequence-based approach is what lets ELK classify GALEN in well under a second and full SNOMED CT (~300k classes) in a few seconds on a laptop, which is the performance envelope v0 aims into; and the validation-relevant incoherence — unsatisfiability arising from disjointness interacting with existential structure — lives inside EL++. So \"validate in reasonable time\" is not a goal bolted onto a classifier, it is what the fragment was selected to hit.\n\n\"Validate\" here means SEMANTIC coherence, not syntactic profile-conformance. The latter is a cheap gate that also drives profile auto-selection, and conflating the two is how a profile check gets mistaken for a reasoning result.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §2.1 (\"The v0 goal: validate an ontology in reasonable time\"), §9 (`howl validate` is the flagship command), §12 M1." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:24:00.301308Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/ddd6f1e5-a1c8-4965-ab9e-22a50428249f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Coherence validation inside an authoring/CI loop" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "New subsumptions against a committed baseline" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Consumers need the subsumptions a candidate theory newly entails RELATIVE TO a committed baseline, not the full hierarchy — every validation in the driving consumer is a small delta against a large stable TBox. v0 serves this as classify-baseline + classify-candidate + diff, which EL's performance makes viable, and it is also the shape that makes incremental classification worth building later.\n\nTwo properties of the requirement are load-bearing and easy to lose:\n\nThe delta is a difference of ENTAILMENTS, not of taxonomies. `Findings.subsumptions` is bottom-compressed (an unsatisfiable C appears as the single pair (C,⊥)), and differencing compressed forms is wrong in both directions — a newly unsatisfiable C entails C ⊑ B for every B while showing one pair, and a candidate that RETRACTS an unsatisfiability surfaces ordinary pairs the baseline entailed all along. So the delta is computed over `entails-sub` across ordered pairs from the UNION of both named-class signatures, with inert declarations for the union injected into both classifications so every pair is queryable on both sides.\n\nBaseline completeness is a PRECONDITION, not a caveat. Set difference is non-monotone in its second argument, so a silence in the baseline becomes a positive false claim in the output — the one place in this system where a partial result manufactures rather than merely omits.\n\nNot deliverable through the port as frozen: `TBoxInput` carries only `triples`, and `classify` is pure and stateless, so no baseline can be identified or held between calls. This is amendment A3, which must also widen `subsumption_delta` to `Option` — an empty `Vec` means \"an available delta that is empty\", so \"ship it and report unavailable\" is not expressible. Either A3 lands or baseline-diff leaves scope; there is no honest middle.\n\nEvidence: SPEC.md §6.7 (baseline diff), §8.4 mapping table, §8.5 A3, §10 test 16." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T22:25:50.949962Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f4a04dd1-aaac-46ae-bb20-d77ea7676992> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "New subsumptions against a committed baseline" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
